# Repo vs `/work` vs `cfg` registry (four-layer config)

## Configuration registry (production source of truth)

- **`cfg` schema** (Azure SQL / PostgreSQL) owns sites, pipeline profiles, DomainProgram IR, studies, storage endpoints/credentials, reference assets, and action definitions.
- Operators use **`methyl-cfg`** (`import-fs`, `upsert`, `materialize`, `publish-program`, `sync-actions`, `provision-assets`).
- **`methyl-cfg materialize`** writes **non-secret** published objects onto `/work` (and runtime-bundle domain paths). **Credentials never materialize** to shared storage; they are expanded into task `input_json` at schedule time.
- File-backed store for local/CI: `METHYL_CFG_STORE` (default `/work/epimethyl/cfg-store`). See `docs/architecture/config-registry.md`.

## Repository (versioned contracts + CI fixtures)

- **Pipeline profiles / DomainPrograms:** authored in git for CI and as import seeds (`methyl-cfg import-fs`)
- **JSON schemas:** `schemas/config/`, `schemas/domain/` (including `storage_location.schema.json`)
- **Documentation:** `docs/`, `docs/usage/19-config-registry.qmd`
- **CI smoke mirrors:** `workflow_engine/domain/checks/*/configs/project_*.json`

Developers may still point `methyl-workflow-run --program` at repo paths. In **production**, workers read **materialized** paths under `/work` / runtime-bundle after `methyl-cfg materialize` (or release promote + cfg materialize).

## Production release bundle (workers + operators, no git)

Each promoted release under `/work/epimethyl/current/` includes:

```
/work/epimethyl/current/runtime-bundle/
  domain/profiles/*.profile.json     # also refreshed by methyl-cfg materialize
  domain/fixtures/*.program.json
  domain/checks/*/configs/*.program.json
  schemas/  scripts/  deploy/
```

`METHYL_PROFILE_DIR` defaults to `…/runtime-bundle/domain/profiles` via `env/worker.env`.

**Production run examples** (no repo paths):

```bash
methyl-workflow-run \
  --program /work/epimethyl/current/runtime-bundle/domain/fixtures/samd_research.program.json \
  --context '{"projectPath":"/work/projects/my-study/configs/project_Healthy_vs_Disease.json","pipelineProfile":"samd_research"}' \
  --parallel-workers 1 -v
```

Or set `METHYL_PROFILE=samd_research` (name resolves under `METHYL_PROFILE_DIR`).

**Distributed workers** receive `resolvedConfig` in task payloads from instance `actionConfig`; they do not read profiles or programs at claim time when the gateway enriched context at start.

## `/work` layout (operator / cluster storage, not git)

```
/work/epimethyl/              # deployed runtime (releases, venv, env, docker, cfg-store) — worker-readable 0755
/work/site/methyl_site.json   # materialized site (genomes, GTF, caches) — METHYL_SITE_CONFIG — 0755
/work/site/storage_endpoints/ # non-secret endpoint metadata only
/work/genomes/                # reference genomes by species (provision recipes) — worker-readable 0755
/work/cache/                   # shared mapper/enricher caches — worker-writable 0777
/work/samples/{sample_id}/    # flat sample archive (not by laboratory) — worker-writable 0777
/work/projects/<study>/        # study-specific science — worker-writable 0777
  configs/project_*.json       # study manifests only
  data/                        # cohort CSVs
  <project_name>/              # outputs (monte_carlo_runs, …)
```

Phase 0 creates these roots via `scripts/init_work_layout.sh` (also invoked from `bootstrap_epimethyl.sh` / `bootstrap_distributed_workers.sh`). `/work/samples` must stay other-writable so every worker — including Docker-as-root Parabricks — can create and overwrite sample dirs. Do not make `/work/genomes` or `/work/epimethyl` world-writable.

Optional: a small instance context JSON on `/work` that only sets `projectPath` (and study-only overrides). **Do not** copy `*.program.json` to `/work/projects/.../configs/`.

## When implementing or documenting runs

- **Do** treat **`cfg` + `methyl-cfg materialize`** as the production path for profiles/programs/sites.
- **Do** keep credentials in `cfg.credential` (never under `/work/projects`).
- **Do** pass `projectPath` in `--context` pointing at `/work/projects/.../project_*.json`.
- **Do** set `METHYL_SITE_CONFIG` (or install site manifest under `/work/site/`).
- **Do not** treat repo `project_*.json` smoke copies or `tools/methyl-config-editor/configs/` as production source of truth.
- **Do not** ship or document `*.program.json` under `/work/projects/<disease>/configs/` as canonical.

